  {
    "id": "sec-7",
    "title": "HALO: Harness for Always-On Loop Oversight",
    "short": "HALO",
    "level": 2,
    "icon": "evaluation",
    "description": "HALO is a diagnostic tool that assesses the loop completeness of existing systems. It examines the coupling channels of the continuing loop and, for self-evolution that rests on outcome feedback, the five steps of the chain of evidence. In read mode, language-model reviewers read a system's papers and released code and decide whether each channel and evidence step is reported. In run mode, a system's released code runs on fixed inputs with one or more channels or evidence steps removed, to examine how its behavior changes."
  },
